# CH04 — The Walking Furnace. Cinderwake, Ivo, the Foundry Colossus. SC04 is authored.

@scene T03_CLINIC
say worker | How does stopping extraction keep the clinic heated? Tell me that and I'll march with you.
@end

@scene T03_HEAT
say worker | The regulators turned pressure into steady heat. First winter nobody froze. That's hard to argue with.
@end

@scene T03_CHILD
say child | My mum says the pipes sing when it's cold. I think they're complaining.
@end

@scene T03_FOREMAN
if ch:CH04 after
say "Foreman" | Spine's closed unless Quill vouches for you. He built half of it.
end
label after
say "Foreman" | Waterwheel's turning. It's slower. The clinic's warm. I'll take slower.
@end

@scene T03_PIPEFITTER
say worker | Copper for the pipes, brass for the regulators, and heartglass for - well. For whatever's inside the brass.
@end

@scene T03_ELDER
say elder | Before the regulators we burned coal and coughed. After, we stopped coughing. Now you want to take it away?
say dain | No. I want to know what's inside it.
@end

@scene T03_COOK
say baker | Shift stew. Same as yesterday. Same as tomorrow. Warm, which is the point.
@end

@scene T03_TALLY_WALL
say worker | Every mark on that wall is somebody burned, crushed or scalded. The ministry ledger says 'minor incidents.'
say worker | We keep our own count.
@end

@scene T03_INN
say keeper | Canteen cots. Warm pipes under the floor. You'll sleep like the dead, which is a joke we don't make much here.
inn
@end

@scene T03_GARDENER
say farmer | Old cooling garden. The pipes used to run under it. Plants grew all winter. Then they rerouted the heat to the Spine.
@end

@scene T03_PELL
if recruited:C04 after
say pell | You're the ones from Veyr. Ivo said you'd come. Ivo says a lot of things he means to do next week.
end
label after
say pell | Leave the manual. That's all I ask. Leave it so someone else can keep the wheel turning.
@end

@scene T03_PELL_GARDEN
if ch:CH09,!flag:accord_cinder accord
say pell | The temporary wheel is running. Crews rotate the hand crank at the lower sluice.
say pell | It isn't elegant. It's ours.
end
label accord
say pell | Ivo. You read the vault's records. So: the heartglass is alive and the clinic still needs heat. Both.
say ivo | Both. The wheel's governor can take a pressure bypass - the old channel under this garden.
say pell | Then fit it. With the crew watching, so they can do it without you.
@end

@scene T03_IVO_SHOP once
say ivo | Visitors. Mind the bench, that regulator is calibrated to a hair.
say ivo | Converts furnace pressure into steady power. Before these, the town froze every third winter. After them, nobody froze.
say tessa | I've seen that coil before. In Crown Quarry. It was wrapped around the extractor, turning the heartglass pulse into - volume.
say ivo | ...It amplifies the relay signal, yes. Steadier pressure, steadier output.
say tessa | It made the voices louder.
say ivo | What voices?
say dain | The heartglass spoke my name in the quarry. Your coil was on the machine.
say ivo | That's - pressure artifacts do strange things with resonance.
say oriel | That is what the inspector said.
shake 0.6
sfx FX015
say narr | A deep clang shakes the shop. Somewhere up the ridge, a siren begins.
say pell | That's the Spine. The main regulator's gone over pressure.
say ivo | Then it'll vent into the workshops. There are people in the workshops.
say ivo determined | You want to know what's inside my regulator? Come with me and help me keep it from killing anyone.
objective ivo | Enter the Furnace Spine (east gate) and vent the pressure lines into empty chambers.
@end

@scene D04_SHIFT_GATE once
say ivo | Three pressure lines. Red, blue, and the regulator crown itself.
say ivo | Every valve can vent into two chambers. One is always a workshop. Look through the window before you turn anything.
say nera | Empty room, then. Not the one with people in it.
say ivo | You'd be surprised how often that isn't the first thing people check.
join C04
say narr | Ivo's Tools set mines, decoys and field repairs. With five in the party, the extra member waits in reserve. Use Formation in the menu to swap.
objective ivo | Balance the red and blue lines, venting into empty chambers.
@end

@scene D04_OCC_WORKERS
say worker | We're sealed in until the line drops! Don't vent in here!
@end

@scene D04_LOST_WORKER once
say worker | I got turned around in the steam. Which way's the gate?
say nera | West, then south. Follow the catwalk, not the pipes.
set d04_lost
@end

@scene D04_D04_RED
if flag:d04_red done
say narr | The red valve. Its vent can go LEFT or RIGHT. Through the windows you can see who is in each chamber.
choice | Vent into the left chamber -> left | Vent into the right chamber -> right | Leave it -> leave
label left
sfx FX004
say worker | NOT IN HERE!
say narr | You slam the valve back. The workers in the left chamber are shaken, not hurt. Look again.
end
label right
sfx FX010
set d04_red
say narr | Steam roars into the empty right chamber. The red line's gauge drops to the green.
end
label done
say narr | The red line is balanced.
label leave
@end

@scene D04_D04_BLUE
if flag:d04_blue done
say narr | The blue valve. Its vent can go LEFT or RIGHT. Check the windows.
choice | Vent into the left chamber -> left | Vent into the right chamber -> right | Leave it -> leave
label right
sfx FX004
say worker | THERE ARE PEOPLE HERE!
say narr | You close it before the steam reaches them. The right chamber is occupied.
end
label left
sfx FX010
set d04_blue
say narr | Steam vents into the empty left chamber. The blue line settles.
end
label done
say narr | The blue line is balanced.
label leave
@end

@scene D04_COLOSSUS once
music silence
say narr | The regulator crown. The main regulator has torn itself out of its housing and is walking.
say ivo | It's not supposed to be able to do that. It's a regulator. It regulates.
say tessa | It's full of the same thing the quarry was. Whatever's in there is pushing.
say ivo | Three vents light before its boiler sweep. Cold slows it. Defend when all three are lit.
battle B04 noflee
set b04_done
music M022
say narr | The Colossus sags against the wall. Its brass shell cracks, and inside, a cup of heartglass flickers - then dims.
say ivo | That's my design. All of it.
say ivo | I told myself it was a battery. A very good battery.
xp 160
objective ivo | Shut the regulator down by hand in the cooling garden beyond.
@end

@scene D04_SC04 once
say narr | The cooling garden. Workers are already here, arguing over the manual shutdown.
say tessa | Shut every line down.
say pell | The clinic is on the second line.
say tessa | You know what is inside it.
say pell | I know who is inside the clinic.
say ivo | We can turn the lower wheel by hand until the canal clears.
say pell | For how long?
say ivo | I do not know yet.
say pell | That is a better beginning than another promise.
fade out 0.5
say narr | Workers rig a waterwheel at the lower sluice and take turns at the crank. The clinic stays warm. The regulator stays dark.
fade in 0.5
say pell | Go and find out what's in the heartglass, Ivo. Then come back and fix the heating properly.
say ivo | That's not a revolution, Pell.
say pell | It's a better one.
say ivo | Shipping manifest from the regulator office. Heartglass crates, marked for Bellharbor on the Glass Coast.
key K_MANIFEST
chapter CH04
objective ivo | Follow the shipping manifest east to Bellharbor on the Glass Coast.
discover L_T04
rumor | Bellharbor dock workers say the ministry is hunting a forger who turns refugees into 'cargo'.
level_floor 11
warp T03_TOWN from_spine left
@end
